    thinking: "**Investigating Persistent Error**\n\nI\'m still grappling with this persistent error! It seems widespread, manifesting on every page, even those dedicated to handling errors like `_error` and `_not-found`. The only commonality appears to be `RootLayout`, which wraps these pages, specifically the `<AppShell>{children}</AppShell>` structure. I need to focus on this area to uncover the root cause.\n\n\n**Isolating the Redux Provider**\n\nI\'ve made some progress! After changing `<AppShell>` to a simple client component, I\'m now honing in on `ReduxProvider`. It\'s a client component, wrapped by `AuthProvider` (also a client component), and contains the `Provider` from `react-redux` and our Redux `store`. It seems to me, `store` is imported from `@/lib/store`, which imports from `@reduxjs/toolkit` and our reducers. I suspect a problem here...\n\n\n**Pinpointing Prerendering Errors**\n\nOkay, I\'ve hit another snag. The thought process has led me down a few rabbit holes. The `Provider` from `react-redux` shouldn\'t be the issue; it uses `useContext` correctly. I initially suspected `ReduxProvider` and `AuthProvider`, but removing them didn\'t fix things. Then I thought perhaps the error was because I had removed those previously, but they were still there. Now I am verifying the build where I first thought I removed `ReduxProvider`, and re-examining the code in `layout.tsx`.\n\n\n"
