    thinking: "**Analyzing the root cause**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve pinned down that setting `force-dynamic` in `layout.tsx` resolved the `useContext` error during compilation. This strongly suggests that statically prerendering client components which depend on Redux/Auth was the culprit. However, a major snag emerges: `force-dynamic` is incompatible with `output: \'export\'`.\n\n\n**Exploring the dependencies**\n\nI\'ve realized that using `output: \'export\'` means I can\'t use `force-dynamic`, which is a problem. Originally, `output: \'standalone\'` was set, explaining why `force-dynamic` worked! But if Firebase requires static files (which it does, explaining why `output: \'export\'` was chosen), then I need a fix that doesn\'t involve `force-dynamic`. The `useContext` error appeared even after removing providers from `layout.tsx`, and went away when `force-dynamic` disabled SSR. If I remove `force-dynamic` and keep `not-found.tsx`, does it build? Let\'s check! Turns out, pages failed without `force-dynamic` in `layout.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 439953538
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
