    thinking: "**Addressing the Next.js Bug**\n\nI\'ve been wrestling with a Next.js issue, specifically a prerendering snag with `export`. I tried switching the output to \'standalone\' and forcing dynamic rendering in `layout.tsx` to get past the weird error. I am unsure whether doing this in layout.tsx is ideal.\n\n\n**Isolating the Context Issue**\n\nI\'ve traced the \"Cannot read properties of null\" error to a likely culprit: a Hook, such as `useRouter`, `usePathname`, or `useAuth`, being called outside of a functional component\'s scope. My hunch is the React dispatcher is null in this case. I\'m now cross-referencing all of my component code to hunt for these hooks at the module scope level, specifically in `src/hooks/useAuth.ts`, `src/app/search/page.tsx`, and `src/app/page.tsx`.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Prerendering Error**\n\nI am thinking about the scope of the error again, and I now believe the error is happening on all prerendered paths. The issue may be located in `layout.tsx`. I\'m starting to think `useAuth` is not the immediate culprit, even if `useRouter` and `usePathname` are used in modules importing the `next/navigation` library. My next step will be to dive deeper into that layout.\n\n\n"
