  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully resolved the build and compilation errors that were failing the application\'s build process. Here is a summary of the accomplishments:\n\n- **Environment Configuration Fix**: The root cause of the `TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading \'useContext\')` and `<Html>` import errors was a mismatch in the React Server components runtime. The global environment was running the Next.js `build` step with `NODE_ENV=development`, causing Next.js to mistakenly pull the development bundle of React into the production server renderer. I resolved this by enforcing `NODE_ENV=production` at the build execution layer within `package.json`.\n- **Structural Restoration & Feed Setup**: I restored the application shell, including the Redux, Auth, and PWA providers back into the `RootLayout`, and configured a clean `/page.tsx` view.\n- **Component Prop Interfaces**: Fixed a data mismatch where the `LiveBattle` and `GroupVoting` components were being passed the entire `contest` object incorrectly instead of their expected specific individual props (`contestId`, `participants`, `userTrustScore`). I also updated the internal mock definitions so that `submission_data.photos` structure complies with what the UI expects, eliminating the final `\"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading \'photos\')\"` static generation error.\n\nThe application compiles perfectly clean, and the core routing, layouts, and voting feeds are restored and functional."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
